        'mastery_questions'=>"What must be true about the parts in a fraction model? | They are equal in size ; They have different colors ; There are always ten ; They are all shaded | A\nWhat does the denominator tell? | How many parts are counted ; The size or number of equal parts in one whole ; The final answer ; Which operation to use | B\nWhy use a common denominator when adding unlike fractions? | To rename them with the same-sized units ; To make them decimals ; To change their values ; To avoid a model | A\nWhich is a useful reasonableness check? | Compare with benchmarks such as 0, 1/2, and 1 ; Add every denominator ; Ignore the whole ; Change the numerator | A\nWhy should the visual match the question? | It shows the same whole, parts, and relationship ; It makes every answer 1 ; It removes the need to explain ; It changes the values | A",
